Godot 4.1.1 AnimationTree.set_process_callback:
```json
{
        "name": "set_process_callback",
        "is_const": false,
        "is_vararg": false,
        "is_static": false,
        "is_virtual": false,
        "hash": 1723352826,
        "arguments": [
                {
                        "name": "mode",
                        "type": "enum::AnimationTree.AnimationProcessCallback"
                }
        ]
},
```

The issue is likely that the hash of the enum class name changed.

The method `MethodBind::get_hash()` in method_bind.cpp performs the following hash on the arguments and return values:
```cpp
	for (int i = (has_return() ? -1 : 0); i < get_argument_count(); i++) {
		PropertyInfo pi = i == -1 ? get_return_info() : get_argument_info(i);
		hash = hash_murmur3_one_32(get_argument_type(i), hash);
		if (pi.class_name != StringName()) {
			hash = hash_murmur3_one_32(pi.class_name.operator String().hash(), hash);
		}
	}
```
This means any attempt to rename, move or unify an enum will break compatibility in this way.

I think this is a problem that needs to be discussed with the GDExtension team. My personal opinion is sub-types like enum vs int or float vs double should not change the hash, since the underlying data type passed into the function would be the same at an ABI level.

